---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About TVSizeCalc - Why We Built This"
  description="TVSizeCalc is a free, simple tool to help regular people find the right TV size for their room."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 sm:py-16">

    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <div class="text-5xl mb-4">📺</div>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">
        About TVSizeCalc
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-gray dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-5 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">

        <p>
          Buying a TV should be simple. But when you Google "what size TV should I buy," you get pages full of
          THX standards, SMPTE viewing angles, horizontal resolution thresholds — all written for engineers,
          not for someone who just wants to watch Netflix on their couch.
        </p>

        <p>
          TVSizeCalc exists because there's a better way. Two questions. One answer. Done.
        </p>

        <p>
          The math behind the calculator is solid: it uses the widely recommended viewing angle of about 30°,
          which balances immersion and comfort. For 4K TVs, that's roughly 7.5× your distance. For 1080p,
          it's about 5.5×. We round to real TV sizes you can actually buy.
        </p>

        <p>
          No ads. No upsells. No "check out these TVs on Amazon." Just a clean tool that gives you a straight answer
          and sends you on your way. If this helped you pick the right TV, that's the whole point.
        </p>

        <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          The most common TV regret? Buying too small. So if you're on the fence — go one size up.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 text-center">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-xl transition-colors"
      >
        Use the Calculator →
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</Base>
